{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Completed live MCP secrets-only redeploy validation. Rotated self-regenerable /rebar/prod/mcp-hmac-signing-key to SSM version 5 (value not logged). Per operator-driven runbook path, paused rebar-autodeploy.timer, verified rebar-autodeploy.service idle, ran infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh to re-materialize SSM secrets, built mcp, started new blue/green container rebar-mcp-bde9c4e66c7d-8093, verified its MCP_HMAC_SIGNING_KEY matched current SSM by equality+length only (length=64, value not printed), health reported store_present=True, handshake_ok=True, opcert_bound=True, opcert_matched=True, flipped /etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf to 127.0.0.1:8093, reloaded nginx, verified live MCP health, gracefully stopped old rebar-mcp-1f3e1c42c9bb-8092, re-enabled autodeploy and observed clean no-op cycles at bde9c4e66c7d501221ddc91e38507ed13a4879b2. A production /mcp/ authenticated streamable-HTTP request then initialized successfully and called rebar-comment_ticket, writing evidence through MCP to exercise authenticated MCP write/signing path. Public /mcp/ unauthenticated response remains 401 as expected. Observed MCP cutover downtime: none detected; old container stayed live until the nginx flip and new health passed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788785812513081001,"uuid":"75e75587-7215-467f-aeaa-54eddf235094"}